  "notes": [
   {
    "category": "summary",
    "title": "Summary",
    "text": "Critical Vulnerabilities in Apache Log4j Java Logging Library\r\n\r\nOn December 9, 2021, the following critical vulnerability in the Apache Log4j Java logging library affecting all Log4j2 versions earlier than 2.15.0 was disclosed:\r\n\r\nCVE-2021-44228: Apache Log4j2 JNDI features do not protect against a"
   },
   {
    "category": "general",
    "title": "Fixed Software",
    "text": "For information about fixed software releases, consult the Cisco bugs identified in the Vulnerable Products [\"#vp\"] section of this advisory.\r\n\r\nWhen considering software upgrades, customers are advised to regularly consult the advisories for Cisco products, which are available from the Cisco Securi"
   },
   {
    "category": "general",
    "title": "Exploitation and Public Announcements",
    "text": "The Cisco Product Security Incident Response Team (PSIRT) is aware that proof-of-concept exploit code is available for the vulnerabilities described in this advisory."
   },
